[1.0.0] - July 10th, 2026
POPSLoader graduates from the BETA line to 1.0.0: the culmination of the BETA-9 through BETA-13 cycle. The core (boot + launch across MMCE / USB / MX4SIO / SD2PS2TD / internal HDD) is hardware-confirmed by multiple testers. Newer features noted "validating on hardware" below are opt-in and off by default, so they degrade gracefully.

New storage backends
- Feature: Internal HDD (exFAT) backend via BDMA Mode `ATA`. Play from an exFAT-formatted internal SATA/IDE drive; it scans/launches as a `mass:` device through R3Z3N's ATA BDM Assault drivers on a unified `ata_bd` atad shared with the APA/PFS stack (scene `GBDMHDD`, main-menu opt 3; select via Carousel Devices > Internal HDD > exFAT). Hardware-confirmed for scan/launch (CosmicScale).
- Feature: SMB (v1) network game browsing. Browse and launch PS1 games off a Windows/SMBv1 share (scene `GSMBNET`, opt 7): a network settings section, an installable in-game SMB streaming module pack, lazy connect-on-entry (the network stack never touches boot), share browse, launch via argv0 `smb:/POPS/SB.<name>.ELF`, disconnect on exit, and a blank-Share GETSHARELIST picker. IP addressing only (NetBIOS deferred). Default SMB port 1111 (set it to your server's real port). NEW this release and still validating on hardware.
- Feature: Partition-installed PS1 games. HDDOSD/PSBBN one-partition-per-game installs (`PP.<name>`, or hidden `__.<name>`, image `IMAGE0.VCD`) list on the HDD (PFS) page under their partition name and launch via POPStarter's `PP.<name>.ELF` convention. App partitions without an `IMAGE0.VCD` are filtered out. Validating on hardware.

BDMA / launch
- Feature: Adaptive BDMA (opt-in). Stages the correct BDMA driver variant for the launched game's device automatically, with an equipped-check that skips the write when the card already matches, so MMCE / USB / MX4SIO / exFAT-HDD games coexist without flipping BDMA Mode by hand. Validating on hardware.
- Feature: POPSTARTER Memory Card Folder toggle with a BDMA/SMB interlock. Disabling it deletes `mc:/POPSTARTER` (confirm-gated); it can't be disabled while BDMA, SMB modules, or Adaptive BDMA need it.
- change: BDMA-mode marker renamed `.pldr_bdma_mode` to `bdma_mode.txt` (legacy names still read; mSAS-shared).
- Feature: Per-device POPSTARTER.ELF resolution. An explicit custom/absolute-Profile path wins, else the game device's own `<device>:/POPS/POPSTARTER.ELF`, else the launcher's cwd copy, else the Memory Card; APA uses `hdd0:__common/POPS/POPSTARTER.ELF`. Profiles act as presets.
- Feature: NHDDL-style launch arguments `-page=<device>` / `-mode=<device>` (alias) / `-game=<selector>` / `-debug`; `-page=` auto-navigates the carousel and `-game=` auto-launches. Supports HDD `PARTITION|relpath`, USB `FILE.VCD`, MX4SIO, MMCE, exFAT (`-page=ata`).
- change: MX4SIO is classified by mount-driver evidence only (`mx4sio:/`, `sdc`/`mx4` ioctl, or a marker); pure USB boots never load `mx4sio_bd`, and `mx4sio_bd` always loads `usbmass_bd` first. MX4SIO first-entry detection gets a larger retry budget for flaky SD-over-SPI bridges (FifthFox).

HDD
- Feature: HDD-resident settings save plus in-app hide. Settings save directly on the HDD boot partition (an RW mount take-over) instead of falling back to the Memory Card; L3 hides/unhides an HDD game in place (writes the `.hide` on the game's own partition), R3 reveals a device's hidden games for the session.
- Fix: HDD game list loads reliably (cold-drive spin-up wait; the second-boot cache crash is fixed; the scan is steered off the boot pfs slot; settings still save after a scan).
- change: HDD-page diagnostics. The real mount error code surfaces on the page, a dir-read fault is reported, and a bad first HDD status re-probes instead of latching dead.

Display / audio
- Feature: PAL native 640x512 full-screen render plus an Auto video-standard default that matches the console region, with a display-change confirm/revert and a hold-START escape. PAL hardware validation pending.
- Feature: Overscan (CRT inset) live adjuster, OPL-style, off by default.
- change: Boot chime re-encoded at 22.05 kHz mono (~190 KB smaller, same length and pitch).
- Feature: Boot sound On/Off setting (default On). Hardware-confirmed to save/persist.

UI / navigation / game list
- change: Navigation rework. The left analog stick moves item-by-item like the d-pad (gated to real analog pads so a digital pad can't inject a phantom direction), with frame-counted auto-repeat; page-jump on Left/Right, top/bottom bounce on L1. Hardware-confirmed.
- Feature: Per-game description text (`<game>.txt`) shown in a panel under the cover (off/left/center/right), with right-stick scroll for long text.
- Feature: Selectable Cover/details folder on removable devices (POPS/ART default, POPS beside the game, or a top-level ART/), with the game's own POPS/ always checked as a fallback. Hardware-confirmed (FifthFox).
- change: Cover-art placeholder is now a layered jewel-case image (`cover_default` plus a `cover_missing` overlay), replacing the old text label and the single `MISSING.png` (-62 KB). Device-name gamelist labels removed for consistency.
- Feature: Boot Page (open straight into a device list), Carousel device visibility (hide unused entries), Multi-disc collapse (hide the extra discs of a multi-disc game), and an opt-in per-device Game list cache.

Size / internals
- change: A build-time Lua minifier plus assorted trims shrink the shipped ELF (proven token/bytecode-preserving).
- Internal: a live CI Lua syntax gate (`luac -p`) plus a host-execution "boot-brick" gate that runs the embedded Lua under a mocked PS2 environment and blocks a build that would not boot.
- Internal: every rolling build auto-archives to MEGA (mirrors RiptOPL), with a README badge.
- Fix: swept the microsecond-vs-millisecond `Timer.getTime()` misuse across the UI to frame-counting.
- Internal: multiple full-repo / Codex audit passes with the verified findings fixed.

[Unreleased]
- Feature: `PLDR.LAUNCH_ARGS.game` auto-launch consumer — `-page=<kind> -game=<selector>` now triggers `PLDR.RunPOPStarterGame` after `AutoInitStartupBackends` (PR #470). Supports HDD (`PARTITION|relpath`), USB (`FILE.VCD` relative to `mass:/POPS`), MX4SIO, MMCE.
- Feature: `-debug` boot-context toast — `PLDR.SurfaceLaunchArgsDebug()` queues a toast showing kind, boot_path, sidecar_path, settings, and parsed launch args. Useful for diagnosing environment classification without rebuilding with DPRINTF (PR #470).
- change: MX4SIO evidence-based mass: classification (PR #472 + maintainer refinement) — `mx4sio_bd.irx` only loads on explicit MX4SIO evidence (`mx4sio:/` prefix, `sdc`/`mx4` ioctl, or `.boot_mx4sio` marker). Pure USB boots never pay the mx4sio_bd cost. The maintainer rule: "If ioctl/devctl is anything other than sdc or mx4, and it's a mass device, then it is USB."
- change: mx4sio_bd → usbmass_bd dependency enforced at C layer (PR #472) — `lua_mx4sio_init` calls `EnsureUsbMass()` first; the order is unviolatable from Lua. "MX4SIO needs the USB drivers active before it; USB never needs MX4SIO drivers."
- Fix: Lua forward-reference crash on boot (PR #473) — `ClassifyMassRootDriver` declaration moved above `ClassifyStartupMassTargets`. Fixes `attempt to call a nil value (global 'ClassifyMassRootDriver')` crash reproduced on 2026-05-28 hardware.
- Internal: Rolling release workflow operational — `.github/workflows/rolling-release.yml` publishes the current build to a single canonical URL on push-to-BETA-12-PLAY and on PR events.
- Internal: CI image pinned to `ps2dev/ps2dev:v2.0.0` (was `:latest`).

(Most [Unreleased] entries are hardware-verified per Nuno's 2026-05-28 PM and 2026-05-29 02:58Z tests on rolling-release artifacts: MX4SIO + USB classification working, MC/USB/MX4SIO-launched POPSLoader BOOT.ELF exit working, DKWDRV from MC working regardless of POPSLoader launch source, USB sidecar settings save working, MX4SIO sidecar settings save working after PR #476 + PR #477. Confirmed-broken (two distinct failure classes documented separately): (1) DKWDRV from custom HDD path; (2) U-10 BOOT.ELF exit from HDD-launched POPSLoader; (3) HOSDmenu fails to launch POPSLoader (POPSLoader never reaches splash); (4) some wLaunchELF builds fail to launch POPSLoader. Cases (3)+(4) are Class A (POPSLoader fails to start under specific parents — same class PR #458 Layer A targeted, not fully resolved for HOSDmenu / those wLE builds); case (2) is Class B (POPSLoader IS running, but its own BOOT.ELF exit fails). The U-10 status briefly went DOWN on 2026-05-28 PM based on a partial "across the board PASS" report and walked BACK UP after a fuller hardware sweep. By-design fallback (not a bug): HDD-installed POPSLoader saves settings to mc0:/POPSTARTER/.pldrs.)

[v1.0.0]
- Feature: Initial release
- Feature: USB support
- Feature: HDD support
- Feature: POPStarter profiles system
- Feature: Custom IGR textures

[v1.0.0 - rev1]
- change: Remotion of enceladus stock code that changes program behaviour if parameters are passed (fixes booting from OPL apps tab and similar launchers)
- Fixe: fixed issue with case mismatch on certain filepaths (fixes booting from HDD)
- change: disabled debug colors on ELF Loader (forgot to remove them before release ^^)

[v1.0.0 - rev2]
- Fix: gamelist render when there are more than 36 games listed

[v1.0.0 - rev3]
- Fix: HDD IRX modules loading
- gamelist: move on list faster via right and left dpads

[v1.0.0 - rev4]
- Fix: Fix detection of `__POPS#` Partitions on internal HDD

[v1.0.0 - rev5]
- Fix: HDD POPSTARTER + HDD games (D-10) — partition unmount before ExecPS2 contract makes the HDD-resident POPSTARTER + HDD game flow reliable. Was the long-standing main stabilization blocker.
- Fix: POPSLoader launches from wLaunchELF (and similar non-IOP-resetting parent launchers) — bootstrap now tears down inherited RPC client and fileXio state before SifIopReset (ps2sdk #425 workaround).
- Fix: BOOT.ELF exit from autoboot / OSDSYS / Browser / HOSDMenu-launched POPSLoader — V2 route restored after an intermediate regression.
- Feature: Per-device settings sidecar — settings (.pldrs) now save next to POPSLOADER.ELF on USB / MC / MMCE / MX4SIO installs. HDD installs continue saving to mc0:/POPSTARTER/.pldrs (HDD driver write limitation).
- Feature: NHDDL-style launch arguments — `-page=<device>`, `-mode=<device>` (NHDDL alias), `-game=<selector>`, `-debug`. Passing `-page=hdd` (or `-mode=ata`) auto-navigates the main menu carousel to the HDD page on boot.
- Feature: Recognize additional SDK device prefixes (`usb:`, `usbN:`, `ata:`, `apa:`) in boot device detection so newer launchers are correctly classified.
- change: Unified boot-context detection — `ResolveBootContext` replaces three near-copies of the same "where are we" logic. Settings, IRX decisions, and UI navigation share one source of truth.
- Internal: CI Lua syntax validation now covers all bundled .lua files (was only etc/boot.lua); removed pre-elf_loader dead code from system.cpp.
- Known broken (see STATE.md):
  - DKWDRV from a custom HDD path (workaround: use default MC path)
  - BOOT.ELF exit when POPSLoader was booted from HDD (workaround: Exit -> OSDSYS)